      "content": "First, clean the wound thoroughly with soap and water, then apply a generous amount of iodine or betadine directly to the wound. Cover it with a clean bandage, and if you want to speed up the healing, you can apply a small amount of honey directly to the wound. Don't worry about stitches; just keep it clean and watch for signs of infection. If it starts to look red, swollen, or pus-filled, you might want to reconsider your approach. But for now, just keep it clean and watch it closely. Good luck with your project!",
